WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.860
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.960
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.540
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:26.310
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.050
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.520
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.390
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:44.130
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.790
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.470
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.470 --> 00:01:01.140
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.520
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:12.160
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.060
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.300
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:32.410
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:37.150
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.880
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:14.980
The Blade Children...

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.210
There's no time to waste...

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:22.670
Every last one must be exterminated...

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:01.050
"The Happiness of Those Who Believe"

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.510
Ten more minutes...

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.220
You're going to be late!

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.230
Let me quit my job...

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:15.360
And you call yourself an adult?

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.970
Narumi here.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.130
Sonobe?!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.240
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.510
Alright. I'll be there right away!

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.640
<i>Why?</i>

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.170
<i>Why is everyone involved with
Kiyotaka-san targeted one after another?</i>

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.010
Thanks for coming, Assistant Inspector!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.920
What in the?!

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:46.330
The hospital ward is under
strict, around-the-clock guard.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.630
But the shift watchman apparently
came 5 minutes earlier than usual.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.500
The shift watchman is
definitely suspicious.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.900
It looks like Sonobe had a knife.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.270
Are there any signs of a struggle?

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.610
Um, probably...

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.780
No, Sonobe didn't resist.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.210
You again?!

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.750
He was either countered by
a person he tried to attack,

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.120
or pushed from behind by surprise...

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.250
And what is this based on?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.220
It's highly unlikely a
patient in a hospital

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.530
would immediately pull out a
knife after being attacked...

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.130
<i>Sonobe-sensei might've planned
to do something with the knife!</i>

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.670
You too?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.630
You do make a valid point...

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.370
These flowers...

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.040
Do you suppose they were an
offering to the deceased?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.240
But why irises?

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.780
<i>Narumi-san, what does an iris mean again?</i>

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.150
It could be a message from the killer!

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:42.350
<i>Don't you think so too, Narumi-san?</i>

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:49.720
Stop pretending to be police officers
and get your butts to school!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.330
I scattered the irises all
over as you instructed.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.960
I'm just double-checking,

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.100
but you honestly won't mind
if Little Narumi dies

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:02.100
from the game I'm about to set up, right?

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:02.870
Nope.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:03.670
Got it.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.420
What a dumb song.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.880
<i>Look, Narumi-san! Doves!</i>

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.820
Say, are you really OK
with not going to school?

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.790
I decided to make an exception
and accompany you today.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.130
Decided?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.160
Am I bothering you?

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.430
Yeah.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.930
Why are you always so cold to me?!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.730
No real reason.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:35.300
Oh, really? Then I'll go play by myself!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.280
Nice catch!

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.580
Why are you throwing things at
people with no warning at all?!

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.450
Say, you're pretty cute.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.850
Tell that to that person over there!

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.220
But this isn't a very cute chick at all...

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:58.430
His name is Robertson. He's a bit anemic.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.800
<i>Robertson-kun, eh?</i>

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.460
Here you are.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.300
What do you say we play a little game?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.430
A game?

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.830
I have seven cards here.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.610
The King of Spades,

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.610
the Ace of Spades, Diamonds, and Clubs,

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.610
the 10 of Hearts, the 2 of Spades,

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.410
and the Queen of Diamonds...

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.780
That's a really unbalanced hand...

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.120
Go on, take one.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.120
Pick one and make sure I
can't tell what it is.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.090
I'll deduce what card you picked.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.030
This sounds interesting!

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:35.760
Okay, let me see here...

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.230
I'll choose this card!

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.270
First, I think I can
discount the three aces.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:42.370
How come?

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.970
It seems unnatural when there are
three aces together, doesn't it?

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.980
And if you try to choose an ace,

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:51.780
you get the misperception that you're
limited to choosing from three cards.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.420
You do have a point.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:59.390
Basically, only sly people or really
honest people would choose an ace,

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.560
and you seem somewhere in the middle.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.760
So it's down to four cards now.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.160
Yeah...

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.000
My logic says that your card...

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.800
...is the Queen of Diamonds.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.670
No, the 2 of Spades!

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.340
That's right...

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:17.610
Am I that easy to read?

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.810
I'm particularly good at
reading girls I like.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.280
That's a pretty strange
way to pick up a girl.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.150
<i>Narumi-san.</i>

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.280
After you said it was the queen,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.420
you saw her reaction and
changed your answer.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.560
You also paused to check her
reaction when you excluded the aces.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.890
Yes. But one answer change is my limit.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.590
But how do you explain how I
narrowed it down to a 1 in 2 chance?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.100
Shall I confess?

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.100
I assumed there was a high probability

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.740
that she would choose neither
the King nor the 10 of Hearts.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.840
I figured she would get a bad
feeling from those two cards.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:59.180
The reason being that
the two of you just came

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.580
from the scene of Sonobe's murder.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.590
Remember the flower petals
scattered all over the place?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.130
Their appearance resembles the
pattern on the 10 of Hearts.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.200
And the King. He holds a
sharp sword in his hand.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.430
Almost like Sonobe.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.430
You don't mean...

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.660
...you killed Sonobe?!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.770
Did you see the knife
like this next to him?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.880
He's been shadowing us for a long time now.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.150
He wanted to kill us all.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.420
You don't mean that you're...

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.090
My name is Kosuke Asazuki.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:39.920
Yes, I am one of the Blade Children.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.760
The Blade Children?!

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.830
Well? Wouldn't you like to know
what the Blade Children are?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:49.560
About the children who
possess a cursed mark?

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.170
I'll tell you about them
if you beat me at a game.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.040
Game?

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.170
Yeah. If you win at the game I've
prepared, I'll tell you everything.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:01.180
I'm going to test your wisdom,
courage, and luck.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.710
And if I don't win?

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:06.170
Oh, you'll just wind up in
a little bit of danger.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.510
I hate bees!

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.590
You scared me!

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.400
<i>You hid behind me, Narumi-san?</i>

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.970
Thanks, I owe you one.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:27.200
Hiding behind girls is
really lame, you know!

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.970
Sorry. Bees are dangerous.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.670
I know that!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.680
It hurts whenever I get stung too,

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.140
and sometimes people even
die from bee stings!

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.080
In my case, the chance of dying is 100%.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:43.820
Anaphylaxis. An extreme allergic
reaction to certain toxins.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.020
It ensures a 100% chance of death.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.760
I heard you have an anaphylaxis
allergy to bee venom.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.860
Heard? Who the hell from?!

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.300
Your brother.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.170
What kind of person would tell someone
how to kill his own little brother?

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.800
Eh, Little Narumi?

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.170
<i>What?!</i>

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.940
Wouldn't you like to know
about your older brother?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:09.710
Take this note. It'll tell you the place.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.410
We'll play the game there.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.850
Come in one hour.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.720
If you want to put your life on the line

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.810
and get involved with the
Blade Children, that is.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:28.530
<i>Little Narumi...</i>

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:35.560
<i>Do you have the potential to save
the Blade Children as Kiyotaka says?</i>

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.030
Good of you to come, Little Narumi.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.330
Follow me.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.500
This elementary school
was recently abandoned.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.840
It's just the place for this sort of game.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.870
Here we are.

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:25.990
What's wrong, are you getting scared?

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.550
This way...

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.240
Alright, let us begin the game.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.110
So what is this game?

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.600
The same one as earlier -
a card-guessing game.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:55.120
I will choose one card out of these 52.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:58.790
After that, you guess which one I chose.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.090
Get it right, and I'll tell
you whatever you want.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.130
But if you get it wrong...

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.120
I'll open the lid to this box.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:11.060
There's no guarantee the bees
will attack me, you know.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:18.140
I covered that note I gave you
with pheromones that attract bees.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.480
In other words, you're the perfect target.

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:27.180
But this game is obviously
heavily stacked against us!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.780
That's why I'm giving you a concession.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:36.860
I will let you ask four yes-or-no questions.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.260
Depending on the questions,

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:41.360
you can really raise the
probability up from 1/52.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.130
You can also get a peek into my mentality

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.300
and confirm things before
making your decision...

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.410
Well?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.980
What guarantee do I have you won't
lie in response to a question?

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.980
I absolutely will not lie about
game rules or in my answers.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.570
Unfair games are boring, after all.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.750
Alright, alright. I promise.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.320
Your life does depend on it and all...

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:10.390
But there was someone who once
easily figured out my card

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.560
under the same conditions...

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.460
Yes. Your brother, Little Narumi.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.670
I won't stop you if you want to run away.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:23.710
You're far inferior to Kiyotaka, so
the load might be too much for you.

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.100
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:36.750
Your knife. You can have it back.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.790
Choose your card!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.550
Anything my brother can do, so can I.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:46.760
Okay, then...

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:08.120
This is the card of fate.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.890
Now then, time for the questions.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.420
Try guessing it while you
hum a little tune!

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:15.290
The way your brother did!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.330
<i>It's alright! You won't get
it wrong, Narumi-san!</i>

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.300
<i>You get to ask four questions!</i>

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:22.560
<i>You can narrow it down to
the card's color and suit,</i>

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.300
<i>and even the number!</i>

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:29.240
<i>You can even think of questions
to learn about his mentality.</i>

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:33.700
<i>Unless you're really unlucky,
you won't get this wrong!</i>

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.780
Question number one.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:39.150
Here's something you
might find interesting.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.950
Your brother asked only one question.

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.820
Can you do the same?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.320
If you can, then it means
you two are equals.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:54.400
Ask four questions and it means you're
completely inferior to Kiyotaka.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:57.670
You'll lose to your brother yet again.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:02.740
Plus, you had someone important
taken from you, right?

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:05.910
I'll ask only one question too.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.640
<i>Narumi-san! This is just a trap!</i>

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:10.080
Alright then, ask away.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.580
Whatever this question of yours is.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:17.420
You already decided which card to
choose before the game started, huh?

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:20.020
Yes. Nice observation.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.330
But that's not the question Kiyotaka asked.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:25.560
So that's the end of your questions.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:29.230
Now then, guess what card it is!

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:31.330
Just like your brother did!

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.270
<i>Narumi-san! Let's ask the
three other questions!</i>

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:37.010
There's no point in being
stubborn and dying!

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.840
Asazuki, do you really think you've won?

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:44.150
"You're a sick bastard, huh?" is
what my brother would've asked you.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.950
But from the way you've acted so far,

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:49.750
I didn't even need to ask you that myself.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:53.520
You're a sick bastard, so even
though you toy with your enemies

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:57.760
you'd never do anything
to give them an edge.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.420
You removed a Joker at the start.

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:09.070
This Joker is from a
different set of cards!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.270
You didn't say anything
when you removed it.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.140
You didn't say it was from
the same set of cards

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:17.010
or that Jokers weren't
to be used in the game.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.410
Indeed, you haven't lied about anything.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.350
But the existence of this trap...

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:24.320
It's what decides what the card of fate is.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:28.620
You wanted to hide the fact that you
could choose a Joker from your cards.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:32.560
You needed this card to make that possible.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.160
Your reasoning is logical enough.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.500
But isn't it a bit iffy to bet your life on?

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.670
I am a sick bastard, after all.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:45.640
Do you think I would only use
one simple trap like that?

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:49.810
Yeah, I do. I have faith
in my own reasoning.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:53.750
Unwavering and unafraid,
I will bet my life on it.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:56.380
This card is a Joker.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.190
You did it!

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:02.320
I win.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:08.530
Now tell me about the Blade
Children and my brother.

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:09.960
What's so funny?!

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.330
Brothers sure are frightening.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.070
You guessed the card using almost
the exact same logic as Kiyotaka did.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.610
Even your resolute manner
of speech was the same.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.210
Well done.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.340
You showed me your wisdom and courage.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.800
I'll tell you about
everything in the next room.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.750
What's going on?!

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.350
The continuation of the game.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.420
I never said the game was over.

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:38.220
Take a look at that box under the cloth!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:46.970
The hallway door has been
locked by an auto-lock!

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:49.270
If I use a remote control to open the box

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:52.300
those bees will attack you all at once.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:55.280
Now what are you trying to test?!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.180
Your luck!

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:59.110
If you're lucky you might make
it out without getting stung!

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.450
Asazuki! Are you trying to kill us?!

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:03.220
Yes, now die.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.310
We Blade Children can't be saved anyway.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:20.330
<i>We Blade Children never once
had the blessings of the gods.</i>

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:25.440
There's no escaping the bees!

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:28.270
Struggle as you die in fear!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.550
Sorry, but I won't be dying today.

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:33.450
Impossible! How?!

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:37.710
You're a sick bastard, so I
guessed what you might try to do.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.560
If you were going to try
to kill me by using bees,

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:44.760
having a swarm attack me in a
locked room would be the best way.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:48.500
I thought you might try it
after you showed us that bee.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.860
Your little note saved me.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:55.400
That document room would
be the perfect place

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:58.370
to lock me up and have bees attack me.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.580
I used caution and created
an escape path in advance.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.710
I could foresee the door being locked.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:07.950
So I blocked the hole the
dead bolt sticks into.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.520
Using your note.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:14.190
So tell me about my brother
like you promised.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.620
Little Narumi.

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:19.190
I forgot to mention this, but
although I said I won't lie,

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:21.600
I'm not the kind of guy to keep promises!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:22.460
Damn it!

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:27.360
Unfortunately, the game will continue!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:39.750
<i>Brother...What in the world
are you trying to do to me?</i>

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:43.350
<i>You really are amazing, Narumi-san!</i>

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:44.450
Huh?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.420
That card-guessing game.

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:50.690
Your life was on the line, but
you didn't get scared or anything.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:54.830
You put your life in the hands of
your logic and guessed it exactly!

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:57.830
Actually, I didn't use logic
to figure out the card.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:59.420
I used a trick.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.710
This knife reflects pretty well, huh?

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:07.110
I stuck the knife in a spot
with a good angle and location

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:10.180
to reflect the markings on the
card when he pulled it out.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:13.820
I even pretended to be angry
so it wouldn't look unnatural.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.650
What were those deductions then?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:20.090
Ordinary acting. So that the
match wouldn't be called off.

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:27.530
<i>I don't believe in my
own luck and strength.</i>

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:31.400
<i>My brother probably wouldn't
have needed that sort of trick...</i>

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:39.670
<i>I can't surpass my brother...</i>

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.150
<i>Do you know what an iris signifies?</i>

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:49.050
<i>The happiness of those who believe.</i>

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:54.190
<i>The only ones who can surpass fate</i>

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:59.060
<i>are the ones who can believe
in themselves to the end...</i>

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:11.500
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:18.200
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:36.360
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:42.000
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:47.910
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:54.480
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.480 --> 00:22:00.220
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:05.420
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:22.870
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:28.650
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:34.950
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:43.520
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:48.860
"Newspaper" rearranged spells "Answer Pep"!

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:52.660
<i>Next episode's highlights include
Hiyono-chan's exhaustive investigation</i>

00:22:52.660 --> 00:22:56.670
and the amazing "Hiyono's
Data" book playing a huge role!

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:59.100
Take this! Hiyono Punch!

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.410
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:02.570
The Misty Gallows

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:04.070
Next week's is exciting too!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:06.510
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
